russian forces hit the central square of  ukraine's second largest city on the  sixth day of war as the attack left  buildings near the local government  headquarters in ruins  residential areas have also come under  heavy shelling as russia hit  non-military targets  the news agency story full set it  corroborated and verified the location  of this footage the surveillance video  appears to show a series of explosions  outside an apartment complex in kharkiv  as several people ran for cover  [Music]  homes were destroyed and the city's  governor said on monday that at least 10  civilians were killed as continued  shelling interfered with rescue efforts  many residents concerned about the  attacks took cover in makeshift shelters  and basements  um  as the violence has escalated the united  nations said more than half a million  people have fled ukraine and the number  could rise to 4 million in the coming  weeks the scale of civilian casualties  and damage  to civilian infrastructure even in these  very early days  is alarming  russian president vladimir putin said no  strikes targeting civilians were carried  out and blamed what he called ukrainian  nationalists for attacking residential  areas according to state media  russia didn't seize any major ukrainian  cities but new satellite images showed a  nearly 40-mile long convoy moving closer  to kiev on monday as talks between  delegations from russia and ukraine on a  potential ceasefire ended with no deal  so even though both delegations appeared  to be sending positive signals and  agreed to another round of talks the man  who launched the war  seems to not yet be backing down we're  not yet sure when these next round of  talks are going to take place but what  we do know is that ukraine is showing  strong resistance and has dug into  defended cities
 

